@startuml State_Order
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

title SALESTORM – Order Lifecycle State Diagram

[*] --> CREATED : checkout creates order\n(linked to reservation)

CREATED --> PAYMENT_PENDING : payment initiated

PAYMENT_PENDING --> CONFIRMED : payment.succeeded\n(event, idempotent)
PAYMENT_PENDING --> CANCELLED : payment.failed\nOR reservation expired

CONFIRMED --> PROCESSING : fulfilment accepted\n(pick & pack)
CONFIRMED --> CANCELLED : customer cancels\n/ refund + release stock

PROCESSING --> SHIPPED : courier picked up\n(AWB assigned)
PROCESSING --> CANCELLED : out-of-stock at warehouse\n/ refund (compensation)

SHIPPED --> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY : courier webhook
OUT_FOR_DELIVERY --> DELIVERED : courier webhook\n(proof of delivery)
OUT_FOR_DELIVERY --> SHIPPED : delivery attempt failed\n(re-attempt)

DELIVERED --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]

note right of PAYMENT_PENDING
  Recovery: if Order Service is down when
  payment succeeds, the order stays here
  until the Kafka event is redelivered or the
  OrderReconciler re-drives it.
end note

note left of CANCELLED
  Cancellation after CONFIRMED triggers
  compensation: payment refund +
  reservation release (if not shipped).
end note

note bottom of DELIVERED
  Implemented with the **State pattern**: each state class
  allows only its legal next states; illegal transition =>
  IllegalStateTransitionException. Persisted with optimistic
  locking (version column) + guarded UPDATE ... WHERE status = ?
end note
@enduml
